    <li>\(\ce{2NO}(g)+\ce{Cl2}(g) \rightleftharpoons \ce{2NOCl}(g) \hspace{20px} K_c=4.6&times;10^4\); [NO] = 1.00 <em>M</em>, [Cl<sub>2</sub>] = 1.00 <em>M</em>, [NOCl] = 0 <em>M</em></li>
    <li>\(\ce{N2}(g)+\ce{O2}(g) \rightleftharpoons \ce{2NO}(g) \hspace{20px} K_P=0.050\); initial pressures: NO = 10.0 atm, N<sub>2</sub> = O<sub>2</sub> = 5 atm</li>
</ol>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/13.E:_Fundamental_Equilibrium_Concepts_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_29"><span id="S13.2.13"></span><h3 id="S13.2.13-44118">S13.2.13</h3>

