<p>Calculate the number of moles of HI that are at equilibrium with 1.25 mol of H<sub>2</sub> and 1.25 mol of I<sub>2</sub> in a 5.00&minus;L flask at 448 &deg;C.</p>

<p class="mt-align-center">\(\ce{H2 + I2 &#8652; 2HI} \hspace{20px} K_c=\textrm{50.2 at 448 &deg;C}\)</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/13.E:_Fundamental_Equilibrium_Concepts_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_104"><span id="Q13.4.17"></span><h3 id="Q13.4.17-44118">Q13.4.17</h3>

<p>What is the pressure of BrCl in an equilibrium mixture of Cl<sub>2</sub>, Br<sub>2</sub>, and BrCl if the pressure of Cl<sub>2</sub> in the mixture is 0.115 atm and the pressure of Br<sub>2</sub> in the mixture is 0.450 atm?</p>

<p class="mt-align-center">\[\ce{Cl2}(g)+\ce{Br2}(g)&#8652;\ce{2BrCl}(g) \hspace{20px} K_P=4.7&times;10^{&minus;2}\]</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/13.E:_Fundamental_Equilibrium_Concepts_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_105"><span id="S13.4.17"></span><h3 id="S13.4.17-44118">S13.4.17</h3>

<p><em>P</em><sub>BrCl</sub> = 4.9 &times; 10<sup>&minus;2</sup> atm</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/13.E:_Fundamental_Equilibrium_Concepts_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_106"><span id="Q13.4.18"></span><h3 id="Q13.4.18-44118">Q13.4.18</h3>

<p>What is the pressure of CO<sub>2</sub> in a mixture at equilibrium that contains 0.50 atm H<sub>2</sub>, 2.0 atm of H<sub>2</sub>O, and 1.0 atm of CO at 990 &deg;C?</p>

<p class="mt-align-center">\[\ce{H2}(g)+\ce{CO2}(g)&#8652;\ce{H2O}(g)+\ce{CO}(g) \hspace{20px} K_P=\textrm{1.6 at 990 &deg;C}\]</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_OpenStax/13.E:_Fundamental_Equilibrium_Concepts_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_107"><span id="Q13.4.12_2"></span><h3 id="Q13.4.12-44118">Q13.4.12</h3>

